 Europe to be down a  bit this year I get and that's based on  though the weakening of the Sterling  because it breaks it so I'm glad I'm  glad you mentioned 2017 let's take us  forward now because you're indicating to  dozens if you might be a little bit  softer i underst  and basically based on your new  initiatives that's autonomous vehicles  electric people's things like that tell  us about those plans and what they will  do to your bottom line well when we look  at 2017 we're gonna have another good  year at Ford it will be a bit down from  last year and the reason for that is  we're we're because we're investing in  emerging opportunities around  electrification autonomous vehicles and  mobility which will open up more growth  opportunities for us down the road so  we're investing for the medium in the  long term but still putting in a very  good year that we're projecting for 2017  so mark one of the things that you'll be  dealing with in 2017 is a new president  and as I mentioned already you've met  with him twice already he mentioned even  in the Roosevelt Room that second  meeting that he'd seen you twice in two  days so first of all just give us a  sense now as you've dealt with him as  president what sort of a person is he  going to be how is it gonna be to do  business with her what do you learn from  those meetings well I think the  president is going to be very good for  business in the economy and first and  foremost is because he's focusing on it  David I think it is very very positive  that his first couple of meetings in his  new administration under his new  presidency he was focusing on  manufacturing and automotive and he's  going to be very focused on driving  policies that will drive looking to  drive investment and job creation in  overall in American manufacturing and in  automotive manufacturing so I think it's  a very positive that he's focused on the  economy and he's listening and he's  understanding from our standpoint well  you know 